  "generated_text": "1. Consider the function \\( f(x) = \\frac{5^x - 1}{5^x + 1} \\).\n2. Evaluate \\( f(-x) \\):\n   \\[\n   f(-x) = \\frac{5^{-x} - 1}{5^{-x} + 1}\n   \\]\n3. Simplify \\( f(-x) \\):\n   \\[\n   f(-x) = \\frac{\\frac{1}{5^x} - 1}{\\frac{1}{5^x} + 1} = \\frac{\\frac{1 - 5^x}{5^x}}{\\frac{1 + 5^x}{5^x}} = \\frac{1 - 5^x}{5^x + 1}\n   \\]\n4. Compare \\( f(-x) \\) with \\( f(x) \\):\n   \\[\n   f(-x) = -\\frac{5^x - 1}{5^x + 1} = -f(x)\n   \\]\n5. Since \\( f(-x) = -f(x) \\), the function \\( f(x) \\) is an odd function.\n\n\\(\\boxed{\\text{odd}}\\)",
  "grade": {
    "error": null,
    "extracted_answer": "[odd, '\\\\text{odd}']",
    "gold_answer": "We have that\n\\begin{align*}\nf(-x) &= \\frac{5^{-x} - 1}{5^{-x} + 1} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1 - 5^x}{1 + 5^x} \\\\\n&= -\\frac{5^x - 1}{5^x + 1} \\\\\n&= -f(x),\n\\end{align*}so $f(x)$ is an $\\boxed{\\text{odd}}$ function.",
    "is_correct": true
